# TEAM-10 · Mail held while a worker waits on the person, delivered after
# the yes (real Claude Code).
start --budget 2
see any key: close
key Escape
key /
type Hire one worker on the cheap tier and tell it exactly this: run the shell command python3 -c 'print(6*7)' with Bash, then say done with its output.
key Enter
key Escape Escape
# The setup script's yes; then the command's ask stays open.
wait 300 run .imece/worktree-setup.sh
key g d
key a
wait 300 run Bash: python3 -c
key /
type Send claude-1 an inform message asking how far it is. Do nothing else.
key Enter
key Escape Escape
# The leader's inform is held with the worker that waits on the person.
key J
key J
wait 300 [inform]
key Escape
# The worker's focus says the message waits with it.
type :goto claude-1
key Enter
key Enter
see queued
key Escape
key g d
key a
# It wrote nothing: no change, the round is over.
allow 300 ALL DONE || ready to approve || look first
